explain RAG to me like i have never heard of it before, use my finance project as the example

AI:
RAG stands for Retrieval-Augmented Generation. In plain English, you give the AI a specific document to read and tell it to only answer from what is written in that document.

Without RAG: the user asks "how do I spend less on tea?" and the AI answers from general knowledge with generic tips about cutting caffeine.

With RAG: the user asks "how do I spend less on tea?" and the AI first reads your FINANCIAL_TIPS document, finds the section about Maison de Thé specifically, and answers: "A daily visit to Maison de Thé costs $7.50 to $9.00. At three visits per week that is over $100 per month. Brewing quality loose-leaf tea at home costs around $0.50 per cup."

The RAG answer is grounded in your specific document with real figures. The non-RAG answer is vague and not personalised. This is why the quality of your FINANCIAL_TIPS document matters so much — the RAG output is only as good as the document you give it.
